  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "45462873",
      "title": "1_API - Introduction to API",
      "lectureOrder": 225,
      "videoOrder": 225,
      "sourceHash": "2faf7a2ecaf763c82a7431a813c35bde302ef26952d5bddd29ec792d152c940d",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.92,
          "end": 1.49,
          "en": "Hi everyone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.49,
          "end": 5,
          "en": "So from this lecture we'll start working with API development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.03,
          "end": 10.37,
          "en": "I will try to cover all the basics of API development with Laravel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.46,
          "end": 20.33,
          "en": "But before we start, we have to at least get an idea of what is API or application programming interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 20.36,
          "end": 26.9,
          "en": "Now, API is a set of rules and protocol that allows different software application to communicate with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 26.9,
          "end": 27.77,
          "en": "each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 27.8,
          "end": 35.84,
          "en": "It defines how requests are made, how data is exchanged, and how responses are returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 35.87,
          "end": 45.71,
          "en": "API are used to integrate and connect various software components, enabling them to share data and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 45.83,
          "end": 47.12,
          "en": "functionality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 47.15,
          "end": 50.63,
          "en": "Now, as you can see here, I have a small diagram.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 50.63,
          "end": 53.54,
          "en": "So it have three parts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 53.57,
          "end": 58.52,
          "en": "One is the client part, second is the API and third is the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 58.55,
          "end": 62.3,
          "en": "You can think yourself here a client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 62.3,
          "end": 65.45,
          "en": "Suppose you are in a restaurant and you want to order something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 65.45,
          "end": 66.62,
          "en": "Let's say a pizza.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 67.16,
          "end": 71.57,
          "en": "So the first thing that you will do is you will ask a pizza to a waiter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 71.57,
          "end": 73.01,
          "en": "And this waiter will.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 73.03999999999999,
          "end": 74.21000000000001,
          "en": "What this waiter will do?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 74.21000000000001,
          "end": 79.94,
          "en": "This waiter will go to the kitchen and ask the chef to create a pizza.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 79.94,
          "end": 82.7,
          "en": "So when chef is done, he will get the.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 82.76,
          "end": 86.33,
          "en": "Give the pizza to the waiter and waiter will give the pizza to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 86.36,
          "end": 87.26,
          "en": "Exactly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 87.26,
          "end": 91.73,
          "en": "That's how this entire API works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 91.73,
          "end": 93.83,
          "en": "Here we have the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 93.83,
          "end": 98.39,
          "en": "Client is basically the front end of your application, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 98.39,
          "end": 102.14,
          "en": "And the API server is basically cooking your pizza.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 102.32,
          "end": 104.87,
          "en": "Or you can say the chef is the back end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 104.9,
          "end": 109.78999999999999,
          "en": "In our case it will be Laravel which will basically process the data and give the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 109.78999999999999,
          "end": 115.55,
          "en": "And API is working as a middleman, which is basically working as a protocol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 115.55,
          "end": 121.7,
          "en": "Or you can say taking your request and giving you the response from the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 121.7,
          "end": 122.9,
          "en": "That's pretty much it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 122.9,
          "end": 128.66,
          "en": "So when the client will send the request to the API, API will send the request to the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 128.66,
          "end": 132.98,
          "en": "Server will process that request and come up with some sort of response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 132.98,
          "end": 138.32,
          "en": "It will send the response to the API, and the API will send the response to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 138.35,
          "end": 139.43,
          "en": "Easy as that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 139.46,
          "end": 146.48,
          "en": "Now you can ask when we should use API and why we didn't use it when we work with Laravel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 146.51,
          "end": 152.06,
          "en": "Before now when we work previously, I mean in our previous lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 152.06,
          "end": 155.06,
          "en": "So we created a small project, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 155.09,
          "end": 161.69,
          "en": "In there, we didn't have to use API because it was a standalone application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 161.69,
          "end": 167.27,
          "en": "Everything was inside a single application, like front end, back end, everything routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 167.3,
          "end": 170.69,
          "en": "Everything was in a single Laravel application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 170.69,
          "end": 175.01,
          "en": "So those application basically calls mono monolithic applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 175.13,
          "end": 181.88,
          "en": "And that's mean all the stuff that you need like uh, back end, front end, everything will go inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 181.88,
          "end": 184.46,
          "en": "a single project, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 184.49,
          "end": 187.34,
          "en": "Everything is packed in a single project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 187.34,
          "end": 192.86,
          "en": "So in that case, we don't have to use any kind of third party integration like API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 192.89,
          "end": 197.81,
          "en": "We don't have to create the API for those sort of application when we need the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 198.05,
          "end": 198.56,
          "en": "API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 198.77,
          "end": 208.49,
          "en": "We need the API when we have two different applications like uh, like in case we are using Vue, react,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 208.49,
          "end": 213.07999999999998,
          "en": "angular or flutter type of stuff as our frontend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 213.07999999999998,
          "end": 216.44,
          "en": "And in the backend, let's say we are working with Laravel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 216.44,
          "end": 222.17000000000002,
          "en": "So those uh, those application types are different in the frontend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 222.17000000000002,
          "end": 225.74,
          "en": "If let's say I'm using react and in the backend I'm using Laravel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 225.74,
          "end": 228.32,
          "en": "So these two are different application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 228.32,
          "end": 231.26,
          "en": "One is the front end application which is made with react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 231.44,
          "end": 235.7,
          "en": "And react is made with JavaScript as you know, and back end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 235.7,
          "end": 237.47,
          "en": "In the back end we are using Laravel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 237.47,
          "end": 240.11,
          "en": "And Laravel is made with PSV.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 240.26,
          "end": 246.8,
          "en": "So both are totally different application built with different stack as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 246.8,
          "end": 253.79,
          "en": "So for make communication between these two we need some sort of third intermediate media.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 253.82,
          "end": 258.23,
          "en": "In our case it will be API not our case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 258.23,
          "end": 261.44,
          "en": "Most of the case it is it will be API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 262.34,
          "end": 264.46,
          "en": "So what this API will do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 264.46,
          "end": 267.49,
          "en": "It will work as a work, as a middleman, as I said.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 267.49,
          "end": 273.07,
          "en": "Or you can say it will basically glue the front end and the back end portion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 273.07,
          "end": 282.01,
          "en": "Or you can say client and the server together, and we will be able to share requests and responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 282.01,
          "end": 286.3,
          "en": "between server and client easily through this API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 286.33,
          "end": 292.81,
          "en": "Another great thing about this API is that your client can be changed any time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 293.2,
          "end": 295.96,
          "en": "Or you can say client can be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 295.96,
          "end": 299.8,
          "en": "It can be a web application or a mobile application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 299.83,
          "end": 305.59,
          "en": "You can use the same API for consume your back end features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 306.07,
          "end": 312.49,
          "en": "This means if you create an API for your back end application, you don't have to worry about your front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 312.52,
          "end": 313.15,
          "en": "end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 313.75,
          "end": 319.3,
          "en": "You can use any kind of app in the front end that supports, uh, API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 319.33,
          "end": 325.12,
          "en": "Or you can say at last it can send any send request and receive response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 325.24,
          "end": 326.47,
          "en": "That's going to be enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 326.47,
          "end": 331.36,
          "en": "So in the front end you can use React View flatter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 331.39,
          "end": 334.09000000000003,
          "en": "It doesn't matter what kind of client you are using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 335.23,
          "end": 340.96,
          "en": "Uh, you can use a same API for consume your all the back end feature without any issue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 340.96,
          "end": 344.08,
          "en": "So this portion will be always the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 344.26,
          "end": 345.79,
          "en": "The client can be different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 345.82,
          "end": 347.26,
          "en": "It can be a web.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 347.38,
          "end": 351.76,
          "en": "Let's say you are you created a front end application with the react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 352.24,
          "end": 352.87,
          "en": "Fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 352.87,
          "end": 355.51,
          "en": "You can use the same API endpoint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 355.51,
          "end": 359.8,
          "en": "Then you think that okay so I need a mobile application as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 359.8,
          "end": 362.74,
          "en": "So with the flutter you create a mobile application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 362.74,
          "end": 369.58,
          "en": "You can still use the same API endpoint for access your back end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 370.3,
          "end": 374.17,
          "en": "I mean the back end feature, you don't have to create anything else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 374.2,
          "end": 380.17,
          "en": "Normally if there wasn't any kind of API features, what we had to do for the web, we have to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 380.2,
          "end": 383.29,
          "en": "a separate back end for the flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 383.32,
          "end": 388.48,
          "en": "For the mobile application, we had to create separate back end as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 388.81,
          "end": 397.6,
          "en": "But now as we have the API, API feature, by that we we can just use the API for communicate with our",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 397.6,
          "end": 404.32,
          "en": "back end without any kind of extra code or extra hassle, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 404.68,
          "end": 406.93,
          "en": "So yeah, that's pretty much it for this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 406.93,
          "end": 412.48,
          "en": "I hope you have a, uh, enough theoretical knowledge about API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 412.48,
          "end": 416.92,
          "en": "And yeah, by the way, before wrapping up, I want to say one thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 417.22,
          "end": 420.4,
          "en": "API responses will be always in JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 420.4,
          "end": 424.27,
          "en": "You have to remember that we'll be talking about this one more in upcoming session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 424.3,
          "end": 425.02,
          "en": "Don't worry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 425.02,
          "end": 431.71,
          "en": "Just I'm putting it in your mind that responses always will be in JSON or XML format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 431.74,
          "end": 435.46,
          "en": "Now I hope you already you already know about JSON.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 435.64,
          "end": 441.85,
          "en": "We already work with the JSON lots of time in our, uh, previous lectures, so I don't think you will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 441.85,
          "end": 443.5,
          "en": "have any kind of issue with the JSON.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 443.5,
          "end": 449.38,
          "en": "But anyways, we'll be talking about that more, uh, later on in the separate lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 449.38,
          "end": 451.75,
          "en": "But yeah, I hope you understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 451.75,
          "end": 456.37,
          "en": "And if you have any kind of question, make sure you to ask it in the Q&A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 456.61,
          "end": 458.23,
          "en": "I'll be there for help.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 458.26,
          "end": 461.32,
          "en": "You and I will be seeing you at the next one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 461.35,
          "end": 461.83,
          "en": "Bye.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
